1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,371
Hello, this is Land Transport Information at Toronto Airport.

2
00:00:04,371 --> 00:00:05,620
How may I help you?

3
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:06,755
Oh, good morning.

4
00:00:06,755 --> 00:00:09,782
Um, I'm flying to Toronto Airport next week,

5
00:00:09,782 --> 00:00:13,945
and I need to get to a town called um, Milton.

6
00:00:13,945 --> 00:00:17,350
Could you tell me how I can get there?

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,091
Milton, did you say?

8
00:00:19,091 --> 00:00:20,396
Let me see.

9
00:00:20,396 --> 00:00:24,312
I think that's about 150 miles south-west of here.

10
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:27,793
In fact it's 147 miles to be exact,

11
00:00:27,793 --> 00:00:33,450
so it'll take you at least say, three to four hours by road.

12
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:33,819
Wow!

13
00:00:33,819 --> 00:00:36,030
Is it as far as that?

14
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:37,085
Yes, I'm afraid so.

15
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:39,987
But you have a number of options to get you there

16
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:43,680
and you can always rent a car right here at the airport, of course.

17
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,108
Right.

18
00:00:44,108 --> 00:00:47,534
Well, I don't really want to drive myself,

19
00:00:47,534 --> 00:00:50,960
so I'd like more information about public transport.

20
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:51,337
OK.

21
00:00:51,337 --> 00:00:55,480
In that case the quickest and most comfortable is a cab

22
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:58,493
and of course there are always plenty available.

23
00:00:58,493 --> 00:01:00,000
But it'll cost you.

24
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,273
You can also take a Greyhound bus or there's an Airport Shuttle Service to

25
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:05,650
Milton.

26
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:10,013
Hmmm, I think for that kind of distance a cab would be way beyond

27
00:01:10,013 --> 00:01:10,637
my budget.

28
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:12,195
But the bus sounds OK.

29
00:01:12,195 --> 00:01:15,000
Can you tell me how much that would cost?

30
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:15,648
Sure.

31
00:01:15,648 --> 00:01:16,943
Let's see,

32
00:01:16,943 --> 00:01:20,829
that would be $15 one way,

33
00:01:20,829 --> 00:01:23,419
or $27.50 return...

34
00:01:23,419 --> 00:01:26,010
that's on the Greyhound.

35
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:26,484
Oh,

36
00:01:26,484 --> 00:01:27,905
that's quite cheap-great!

37
00:01:27,905 --> 00:01:31,220
But whereabouts does it stop in Milton?

38
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:34,585
It goes directly from the airport here to the City Centre

39
00:01:34,585 --> 00:01:35,808
and it's pretty fast.

40
00:01:35,808 --> 00:01:40,091
But you have to bear in mind that there is only one departure a

41
00:01:40,091 --> 00:01:40,397
day,

42
00:01:40,397 --> 00:01:43,150
so it depends what time your flight gets in.

43
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,286
Oh, of course.

44
00:01:44,286 --> 00:01:48,450
Hang on, we're due to get there at 11.30 am.

45
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:52,126
Hmmm, too bad, the bus leaves at 3.45,

46
00:01:52,126 --> 00:01:56,210
so you would have quite a wait-more than 4 hours.

47
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:57,497
Oh, I see.

48
00:01:57,497 --> 00:02:00,500
Well, what about the Shuttle you mentioned?

49
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:00,856
OK.

50
00:02:00,856 --> 00:02:06,193
That's the Airport Shuttle that will take you from the airport right to your hotel

51
00:02:06,193 --> 00:02:07,261
or private address.

52
00:02:07,261 --> 00:02:11,175
It's a door-to-door service and it would suit you much better,

53
00:02:11,175 --> 00:02:13,310
because there's one every two hours.

54
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:15,000
So how much does that cost?

55
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,005
Let's see.

56
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:16,508
Yeah,

57
00:02:16,508 --> 00:02:19,522
that's $35 one way, $65 return,

58
00:02:19,522 --> 00:02:25,050
so I guess it's a bit more expensive than the Greyhound.

59
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:25,375
Oh,

60
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:29,930
that doesn't sound too bad, especially if it'll take me straight to the hotel.

61
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,320
But you do need to reserve a seat.

62
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,195
OK, is it possible to make a booking right now?

63
00:02:36,195 --> 00:02:36,970
Through you?

64
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:37,600
Sure.

65
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:42,031
OK, I just have to fill this form out for you.

66
00:02:42,031 --> 00:02:46,060
So what date do you want to book this for?

67
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:48,706
The 16th of October-oh, no, sorry,

68
00:02:48,706 --> 00:02:50,470
that's my departure date.

69
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:52,674
I arrive on the 17th,

70
00:02:52,674 --> 00:02:55,320
so book it for then, please.

71
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:55,776
So,

72
00:02:55,776 --> 00:02:58,965
that's the Toronto Airport Shuttle to Milton.

73
00:02:58,965 --> 00:03:02,610
And this is for just one person or...

74
00:03:02,610 --> 00:03:02,660
?

75
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:04,390
Yes, just me, please.

76
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:04,732
Right.

77
00:03:04,732 --> 00:03:08,492
And you said your expected time of arrival was 11.30?

78
00:03:08,492 --> 00:03:13,278
So if I book your Shuttle for after 12.00- let's say, 12.30:

79
00:03:13,278 --> 00:03:18,064
that should give you plenty of time to, you know, collect your baggage, maybe

80
00:03:18,064 --> 00:03:19,090
grab a coffee?

81
00:03:19,090 --> 00:03:19,411
Yeah,

82
00:03:19,411 --> 00:03:22,620
that sounds fine, as long as we land on time!

83
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:27,105
Well, we'll take your flight details so you don't need to worry too much

84
00:03:27,105 --> 00:03:27,745
about that.

85
00:03:27,745 --> 00:03:29,347
Now, what about the fare?

86
00:03:29,347 --> 00:03:31,589
What sort of ticket do you want?

87
00:03:31,589 --> 00:03:32,550
One way or...?

88
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:32,878
Yes,

89
00:03:32,878 --> 00:03:37,140
that'll be fine, provided I can book the return trip once I'm there.

90
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:41,787
NO problem-just allow a couple of days in advance to make sure you get

91
00:03:41,787 --> 00:03:42,450
a seat.

92
00:03:42,450 --> 00:03:44,110
And what's your name, please?

93
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:46,340
Janet, Janet Thomson.

94
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:48,930
Is that Thompson spelt with a 'p'?

95
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:53,180
No, it's T-H-O-M-S-O-N.

96
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:53,568
OK.

97
00:03:53,568 --> 00:03:56,284
And you'll be coming from the UK?

98
00:03:56,284 --> 00:03:59,000
What flight will you be travelling on?

99
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:05,810
Oh, it's Air Canada flight number AC936, from London Heathrow.

100
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:06,176
Right.

101
00:04:06,176 --> 00:04:09,103
Now, do you know where you'll be staying?

102
00:04:09,103 --> 00:04:12,030
We need to give the driver an address.

103
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:21,295
Yes, it's called the Vacation Motel-and I think it's near the town centre.

104
00:04:21,295 --> 00:04:27,710
Anyway, the address is 24, Kitchener Street-that's KITCHENER Street.

105
00:04:27,710 --> 00:04:28,582
That's fine.

106
00:04:28,582 --> 00:04:29,018
Right,

107
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:31,633
so that's $35 to pay please.

108
00:04:31,633 --> 00:04:35,120
Have you got your credit card number there?

109
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:40,266
Yes, it's a VISA card,

110
00:04:40,266 --> 00:04:48,500
and the number is 3303 8450 2045 6837.

111
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:48,829
OK.

112
00:04:48,829 --> 00:04:49,159
Well,

113
00:04:49,159 --> 00:04:50,806
that seems to be everything.

114
00:04:50,806 --> 00:04:54,760
Have a good trip and we'll see you in Toronto next week!

115
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:57,750
Yes, bye-oh, thanks for your help!
